{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwNHy7eAjvaCWQo3EoZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard to check how the panels look, and I haven't seen the rule run.\n\n**Data:** The Kibana Sample Data Logs view indexes web requests, with `timestamp` as the time field. The fields I used are:\n- `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as a string)\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src`\n\nIt also has `clientip`, `host`, `machine.os`, `request` and `url`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-778dd095 Web logs overview\" has five panels and defaults to the last 7 days. It's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-778dd095-web-logs-overview-81533d980a20. The panels are:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Bytes by file extension\n- Top 10 source countries\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-778dd095 5xx spike\" runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 documents with a `response` starting with \"5\" arrive in a 5-minute window. It uses Kibana's `.es-query` rule type. I enabled it in a separate step, because the create call leaves new rules disabled.\n\nThe rule has no action attached, so when it fires it will show up as an alert in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":155,"cache_read_input_tokens":20409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":155},"output_tokens":451,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"81a29574-c3bb-403c-a3ec-7dacf0434172","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:06:46.947Z","request_id":"req_011CfwNHxt1Q6FBs7RBy1f5Z"}
